# Everything the runner image bakes in.
#
# The point is that a workflow never installs a toolchain. If a job needs
# something, it goes here and the image is rebuilt — not into a
# `run: apt-get install` step that runs on every job forever.
#
# One package per line. Comments and blank lines are ignored.
# `make image-packages` prints the effective list.

# --- runner .NET runtime dependencies (do not remove) ---
ca-certificates
libicu74
libssl3
libkrb5-3
zlib1g

# --- the shim's engine client ---
# Remote client only: there is no engine in this container. A full podman
# would give the runner a second, empty container store, and every job would
# silently re-pull its images into a store the host never prunes.
podman-remote

# --- workflow basics ---
curl
wget
git
git-lfs
jq
openssl
unzip
zip
xz-utils
tar
gzip
locales
tzdata
procps

# --- C toolchain ---
# build-essential is explicit because libc6-dev is a *Recommends* of gcc, not
# a Depends. With --no-install-recommends a slimmed image otherwise yields a
# gcc with no stdlib.h.
build-essential
clang
lld
cmake
ninja-build
pkg-config
autoconf
automake
libtool
bison
flex
gdb
valgrind
ccache

# --- scripting ---
python3
python3-venv
python3-pip

# NOTE: no nodejs. The runner ships externals/node20 and uses it for every
# JavaScript action, so a system Node would not be what actually runs
# actions/checkout — it would just be a second, unused copy.
